   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 62 of the laws of 2011, relating to constituting\nchapter 18-A of the consolidated laws relating to financial services, in\nrelation to extending the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S10579",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S10579-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd Part A §114, Chap 62 of 2011",
    "lawSection": "Financial Services",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S10579\n\nSPONSOR: SANDERS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 62 of the laws of 2011, relating to constituting\nchapter 18-A of the consolidated laws relating to financial services, in\nrelation to extending the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo extend the expiration of the State Charter Advisory Board for 5 addi-\ntional years through October 3, 2031 and to add reporting requirements.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection One: Amends subdivision (e) of section 114 of part A of chapter\n62 of the laws of 2011, as amended by chapter 302 of the laws of 2021,\nis amended to extend the expiration date of section 205-b of the finan-\ncial services law from October 3, 2026 to October 3, 2031.\n\nSection Two: Effective Date.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nAuthorization for the State Charter Advisory Board is set to expire on\nOctober 3, 2026.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe State Charter Advisory Board works with the Superintendent in\nretaining state-chartered banking institutions, encouraging federally\nchartered institutions to convert to a state charter and promote the\nstate banking system. There are nine members of the advisory board,\nconsisting of one representative of credit unions, one representative of\nconsumers, one representative of foreign banks; and representatives of\nbanks reflecting a range of assets, size and geographical location.\n\nThe superintendent governs the method by which state chartered insti-\ntutions may nominate persons-to the board and the process for selecting\nsuch members, provided that the representative of consumers is selected\nby the Superintendent.\n\nThe requirement of an annual report allows the legislature to monitor\ntopics of concern to the industry and consumers and any discussion of\nlegislation that could be requested or appropriate.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Legislation.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
